    "result_text": "The test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` posts an owner with `x@mailinator.com` and expects 400 \u2014 it passed.\n\nDone. I added a single new file, `OwnerDisposableEmailAdvice.java`, following the existing `Owner*Advice` `RequestBodyAdvice` pattern.\n\n**Why this keeps structural impact minimal:** the change is one new, self-contained class with no other methods around the changed logic (WMC_other \u2248 0), rather than editing an existing controller or service. Each method in it is trivial (the only branching lives in `isDisposable`, CC 3), and only one file is touched. It rejects create/update owner requests whose email domain is `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, or `guerrillamail.com` (case-insensitive) with 400, leaving absent emails untouched.\n\n`BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
